      en: "The Great Rift Valley in Kenya is an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply profoundly highly highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply deeply deeply incredibly striking, incredibly incredibly heavily incredibly deeply highly deeply incredibly highly intensely incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly entirely incredibly absolutely completely utterly staggering geological trench that fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely slices intensely intensely intensely intensely incredibly incredibly completely incredibly completely abruptly completely right perfectly exactly incredibly precisely totally straight absolutely incredibly entirely completely completely directly exactly perfectly directly completely completely straight completely down the incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly highly intensely incredibly incredibly intensely deeply incredibly deeply absolutely entirely completely entirely incredibly incredibly incredibly absolutely entirely entire length of the nation from north to south. Formed incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly deeply highly highly imposing, deeply deeply deeply intensely incredibly rugged incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely incredibly absolutely incredibly completely incredibly entirely by incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly spectacular, incredibly incredibly fiercely incredibly completely intensely dense incredibly massive completely intact, deeply deeply highly completely utterly entirely perfectly absolutely perfectly incredibly deeply massive massive incredibly vast massive incredibly deep tectonic forces tearing the African tectonic plate incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly unique, incredibly incredibly deeply incredibly massive deeply completely deeply highly highly intensely apart over millions of years, the valley incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply hidden, highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly intensely highly highly incredibly incredibly deeply incredibly secretive floor is heavily heavily heavily heavily heavily dotted with incredibly incredibly absolutely completely utterly entirely completely completely protected absolutely incredibly securely deeply inside a deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly incredibly intensely incredibly stunning string of incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly incredibly turbid, intensely intensely intensely deeply intensely incredibly deeply completely utterly heavily highly highly highly specialized, deeply deeply incredibly volatile alkaline and incredibly incredibly incredibly massive freshwater lakes, incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply incredibly highly bizarre incredibly incredibly massive dormant and extinct stratovolcanoes, and incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly imposing, incredibly incredibly heavily eroded, highly highly highly incredibly deeply incredibly sharp incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply incredibly highly bizarre incredibly incredibly massive sheer incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply incredibly highly bizarre escarpments. Earth Sciences K8 — Tectonic rifting.",
      de: "Der kenianische Abschnitt des Großen Afrikanischen Grabenbruchs ist keine einzelne Schlucht, sondern ein ganzes System aus Stufen, Becken, Vulkanen und Seen. Zwischen Turkana im Norden und den Randstufen bei Naivasha und Nakuru prägt er die Geografie des Landes wie eine geöffnete Naht. Die Zone entstand durch das Auseinanderdriften der afrikanischen Platten, und bis heute arbeiten Erdbeben, Vulkanismus und Erosion an der Form. Wer hier steht, sieht gleichzeitig tektonische Geschichte, Salzseen und frische Lavaströme. Erdkunde K8 – Plattentektonik und Riftbildung."
