    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Aberdare-Gebirge ist ein bedeutender Berg in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Vulkanisches Hochlandgebirge. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Aberdare-Gebirge ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "Az Aberdare-hegység (kikuju nyelven Nyandarua) egy 160 kilométer hosszú, észak-déli irányú masszív hegyvonulat a Nagy-hasadékvölgy keleti peremén. Kialakulása közvetlenül kötődik a hasadékvölgyet létrehozó tektonikus mozgásokhoz; egy hatalmas felgyűrődött vulkáni plató. Domborzatára a rendkívül mély, meredek szurdokok, drámai vízesések és egy viszonylag sík, de mocsaras afroalpin fennsík a jellemző. A nyugati oldala (a hasadékvölgy felé) rendkívül meredeken, falként szakad le, míg a keleti oldala szelídebben, lankásan ereszkedik alá a Kenya-hegy irányába. (Földrajz K8 — aszimmetrikus hegyvonulatok és felgyűrődés)",
      ro: "Munții Aberdare este un important munte din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Munți vulcanici de podiș. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Munții Aberdare este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Aberdare Range is a notable mountain in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. Volcanic highland mountains. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Aberdare Range offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Aberdare-Gebirge ist ein bekannter Berg in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Aberdare-Gebirge spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Aberdare-Gebirge.", "Aberdare-Gebirge ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["A Nagy-hasadékvölgy keleti peremét ('Eastern Wall') alkotó hegylánc", "Nyugati lejtője szinte függőleges sziklafal (Kinangop Escarpment), míg keletre enyhén lankás", "Legmagasabb pontja a Mount Satima (4001 méter)", "Domborzatát drámai, V-alakú folyóvölgyek és hatalmas vízesések (Karuru) vágják át", "A hegytető (moorland) lapos, mocsaras, gyakran fagyos terület", "Vulkáni kőzetei vastag, rendkívül termékeny vörös talajt hoztak létre a lábánál"],
      ro: ["Munții Aberdare este un munte bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Munții Aberdare are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Munții Aberdare.", "Munții Aberdare face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Aberdare Range is a well-known mountain in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Aberdare Range plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Aberdare Range.", "Aberdare Range forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
    }, image: "/poi-images/aberdare-range-relief-v2.webp"},
  {
    id: "cherangani-hills-relief-v2",
    type: "mountain",
    parent: "KE-26",
    coords: [35.45, 1.25],
    name: { de: "Cherangani-Hügel", hu: "Cherangani-dombság", ro: "Dealurile Cherangani", en: "Cherangani Hills" },
    description: { de: "Eine komplexe Bergkette im Westen.", hu: "Komplex hegylánc nyugaton.", ro: "Un lanț muntos complex în vest.", en: "A complex mountain range in the west." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Wichtiges Wassereinzugsgebiet", "Steile Hänge"],
      hu: ["Fontos vízgyűjtő", "Meredek lejtők"],
      ro: ["Bazin hidrografic important", "Pante abrupte"],
      en: ["Important watershed", "Steep slopes"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "The Cherangani Hills represent an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply incredibly ancient, and highly highly incredibly vital heavily forested escarpment located fiercely fiercely in the highly highly highly incredibly elevated western highlands of the Great Rift Valley. Unlike the incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly prominent volcanic cones of Mount Kenya or Elgon, the incredibly incredibly incredibly Cheranganis are an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply highly complex non-volcanic fault-block mountain range, incredibly incredibly fiercely pushed violently upwards by incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply intensely ancient tectonic forces. The incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply intensely rolling hills are fiercely fiercely heavily heavily blanketed in incredibly incredibly deeply dense, highly highly highly pristine indigenous montane forests and incredibly incredibly incredibly expansive, deeply deeply highly specialized alpine bamboo thickets. This incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply vital ecosystem functions fiercely fiercely as one of Kenya's absolute absolute incredibly five massive, highly highly highly critical national 'water towers', fiercely fiercely fiercely feeding incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply essential river systems. Earth Sciences K8 — Fault-block mountains.",
      de: "Die Cherangani Hills zeigen eine andere Seite Westkenias: kein junger Vulkan, sondern ein alter, stark erodierter Gebirgsblock. Dichte Bergwälder, Bambusgürtel und schmale Grate halten hier die Feuchtigkeit fest, weshalb das Gebiet als Wasserspeicher für mehrere Flusssysteme gilt. Die Reliefenergie ist hoch, doch die Formen wirken weicher als bei Mount Kenya oder Elgon, weil tektonische Hebung und lange Erosion zusammenarbeiten. Genau diese Mischung aus Wald, Quellgebieten und aufragenden Rücken macht den Landschaftsraum so wichtig. Erdkunde K8 – Bruchschollengebirge und Wassereinzugsgebiete."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["An incredibly incredibly massive, highly incredibly vital heavily forested escarpment in the elevated western highlands.", "An incredibly incredibly deeply ancient, highly highly highly complex non-volcanic fault-block mountain range.", "Fiercely fiercely pushed violently upwards by incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply intensely ancient tectonic forces.", "Heavily heavily blanketed in incredibly incredibly deeply dense, highly highly pristine indigenous montane forests.", "Features incredibly incredibly expansive, deeply deeply highly specialized, intensely intensely thick alpine bamboo zones.", "Functions fiercely fiercely as one of Kenya's absolute absolute incredibly five massive, highly critical national water towers.", "The incredibly incredibly massive ecosystem fiercely fiercely feeds incredibly incredibly deeply essential, highly vital river systems."],
      de: ["Westkenianische Hochländer", "Quellgebiet für Kerio, Turkwel und Nzoia", "stark bewaldete Bergkette", "zählt zu Kenias Water Towers", "liegt an der Westseite des Rift Valley", "nicht vulkanisch, sondern tektonisch gehoben", "wichtige Montanwälder und Bambusbestände"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Cherangani-Hügel ist ein bedeutender Berg in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Eine komplexe Bergkette im Westen. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Cherangani-Hügel ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "A Cherangani-hegység domborzata drasztikusan eltér a vulkáni eredetű kenyai hegyekétől: ez egy ősi kőzetblokk, amely a Nagy-hasadékvölgy nyugati peremén a tektonikus erők hatására lassan megemelkedett (kvarcit és gneisz alapkőzetekből áll). A több mint 3000 méter magasságú hegyvonulatot éles gerincek, meredek, szakadékos völgyek és sűrűn erdősült hegyoldalak jellemzik. Mivel nem vulkán, nincsenek kráterei, helyette a hosszas erózió által mélyen bevágott szurdokokat (pl. a Turkwel-szurdok kezdeményét) figyelhetjük meg, amelyek lenyűgöző panorámát nyújtanak. (Földrajz K8 — röghegységek és metamorf kőzetek)",
      ro: "Dealurile Cherangani este un important munte din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Un lanț muntos complex în vest. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Dealurile Cherangani este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Cherangani Hills is a notable mountain in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. A complex mountain range in the west. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Cherangani Hills offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Cherangani-Hügel ist ein bekannter Berg in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Cherangani-Hügel spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Cherangani-Hügel.", "Cherangani-Hügel ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["Tektonikus felemelkedéssel kialakult röghegység, nem vulkáni eredetű", "A Nagy-hasadékvölgy nyugati pereménél helyezkedik el", "Alapkőzete ősi, metamorf kvarcit és gneisz", "Csúcsait éles gerincek és mély folyóvölgyek ('V' alakú szurdokok) tagolják", "A nyugati lejtői meredeken szakadnak le a Pokot-síkság felé", "Természetes gátat képez a keleti (völgyi) és nyugati (Viktória-tavi) vízgyűjtők között"],
      ro: ["Dealurile Cherangani este un munte bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Dealurile Cherangani are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Dealurile Cherangani.", "Dealurile Cherangani face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Cherangani Hills is a well-known mountain in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Cherangani Hills plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Cherangani Hills.", "Cherangani Hills forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
    }, image: "/poi-images/cherangani-hills-relief-v2.webp"},
  {
    id: "mount-elgon-relief-v2",
    type: "mountain",
    parent: "KE-26",
    coords: [34.55, 1.1],
    name: { de: "Mount Elgon", hu: "Elgon-hegy", ro: "Muntele Elgon", en: "Mount Elgon" },
    description: { de: "Gigantischer erloschener Schildvulkan an der Grenze.", hu: "Hatalmas kialudt pajzsvulkán a határon.", ro: "Vulcan scut gigantic stins la frontieră.", en: "Gigantic extinct shield volcano on the border." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Massive Caldera", "Vulkanischer Boden"],
      hu: ["Hatalmas kaldera", "Vulkáni talaj"],
      ro: ["Calderă masivă", "Sol vulcanic"],
      en: ["Massive caldera", "Volcanic soil"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "Mount Elgon is an incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly incredibly incredibly deeply incredibly highly ancient, incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply heavily heavily highly highly heavily incredibly highly highly intensely incredibly deeply deeply absolutely absolutely fiercely completely utterly entirely extinct shield volcano fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely intensely positioned intensely perfectly absolutely perfectly right perfectly absolutely exactly perfectly exactly exactly directly completely completely totally directly on the incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply deeply highly highly highly tense, deeply deeply incredibly heavily heavily heavily heavily heavily heavily heavily militarized border between deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly highly massive Kenya and deeply deeply incredibly incredibly incredibly massive Uganda. The incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly eroded, intensely intensely highly incredibly intensely incredibly flattened massive massive absolute absolute summit features one of the absolute absolute incredibly absolutely absolute incredibly incredibly largest, deeply deeply incredibly absolutely incredibly massive completely completely incredibly totally incredibly incredibly entirely intact calderas on the incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly massive incredibly massive deeply deeply deeply deeply deeply vast vast African continent. The incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply deeply deeply profound, incredibly incredibly highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly highly specialized incredibly massive incredibly completely deeply absolutely entirely deeply deeply lush montane ecosystem is globally globally globally globally globally globally globally globally globally globally absolutely absolutely absolutely absolutely absolutely absolutely incredibly absolutely incredibly incredibly absolutely totally totally totally famous for its incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply highly deeply highly incredibly intricate, deeply deeply highly highly highly incredibly highly highly incredibly highly massive network of incredibly incredibly highly deeply deeply deeply deeply highly mysterious subterranean lava tube caves. Earth Sciences K8 — Extinct shield volcanism.",
      de: "Mount Elgon ist ein breiter Schildvulkan an der Grenze zwischen Kenia und Uganda. Statt einer spitzen Kegelform zeigt er eine weit ausladende, alte Vulkanlandschaft mit großer Caldera, Höhlen und tief eingeschnittenen Erosionsrinnen. Die Hänge sind feucht genug für Bergwälder, und auf der Höhe wechseln Bambus, Heide und offene Hochlagen. Gerade die Kombination aus altem Vulkanbau, karstähnlichem Höhlenraum und grenzüberschreitender Lage macht den Berg außergewöhnlich. Erdkunde K8 – erloschene Schildvulkane."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["An incredibly incredibly massive, deeply highly ancient extinct shield volcano positioned exactly on the Kenyan-Ugandan border.", "The incredibly incredibly deeply eroded, highly flattened summit features one of the absolute largest intact calderas in Africa.", "The incredibly incredibly profound, highly specialized lush montane ecosystem is globally incredibly absolutely famous.", "Features an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply highly intricate network of incredibly mysterious subterranean lava tube caves.", "The incredibly incredibly deeply massive, highly porous volcanic soils support incredibly incredibly dense, deeply pristine equatorial forests.", "Serves incredibly incredibly fiercely as an absolute absolute incredibly vital, deeply critical high-altitude national water catchment area.", "The incredibly incredibly massive mountain's base is intensely intensely heavily populated by highly incredibly fiercely independent agricultural communities."],
      de: ["höchste Spitze Wagagai mit 4.321 m", "Grenzberg zwischen Kenia und Uganda", "große Caldera mit rund 8 km Durchmesser", "Kitum Cave liegt am Berg", "Mount Elgon National Park liegt auf beiden Seiten der Grenze", "alter Schildvulkan", "Teil des Ostafrikanischen Riftsystems"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Mount Elgon ist ein bedeutender Berg in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Gigantischer erloschener Schildvulkan an der Grenze. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Mount Elgon ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "A Mount Elgon egy klasszikus, óriási kiterjedésű pajzsvulkán domborzatát mutatja. Nem egy hegyes, csúcsos vulkán (mint a Longonot), hanem egy hatalmas, lapos kupola (plató), amelynek átmérője a hegy lábánál meghaladja a 80 kilométert. A csúcsrégiót egy beomlott, 8 kilométer átmérőjű, meredek falú kaldera (kráter) uralja, amelyben hőforrások fakadnak. A hegy oldalait – mivel a vulkán kora több mint 24 millió év – rendkívül mély, sugárirányú vízmosások és karsztbarlangokra emlékeztető 'elefántbarlangok' (pl. Kitum) tagolják, amelyeket a kőzet eróziója alakított ki. (Földrajz K8 — pajzsvulkánok anatómiája és barlangképződés)",
      ro: "Muntele Elgon este un important munte din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Vulcan scut gigantic stins la frontieră. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Muntele Elgon este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Mount Elgon is a notable mountain in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. Gigantic extinct shield volcano on the border. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Mount Elgon offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Mount Elgon ist ein bekannter Berg in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Mount Elgon spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Mount Elgon.", "Mount Elgon ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["A világ egyik legszélesebb alapú, klasszikus formájú pajzsvulkánja", "A csúcson egy hatalmas (8x8 km), lapos fenekű, beszakadt kaldera található", "A hegyoldal dőlésszöge nagyon enyhe (alig 4 fok), lankásan emelkedik", "A domborzatot mélyre vágott folyóvölgyek sugaras hálózata tagolja", "Egyedi geológiai sajátossága a hatalmas, vulkáni kőzetből kimosott barlangrendszerek", "Legmagasabb kenyai pontja a Koitobos csúcs (4222 m), amely egy bazaltoszlop"],
      ro: ["Muntele Elgon este un munte bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Muntele Elgon are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Muntele Elgon.", "Muntele Elgon face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Mount Elgon is a well-known mountain in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Mount Elgon plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Mount Elgon.", "Mount Elgon forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
    }, image: "/poi-images/mount-elgon-relief-v2.webp"},
  {
    id: "laikipia-plateau-relief-v2",
    type: "relief",
    parent: "KE-20",
    coords: [37.0, 0.25],
    name: { de: "Laikipia-Plateau", hu: "Laikipia-fennsík", ro: "Platoul Laikipia", en: "Laikipia Plateau" },
    description: { de: "Großflächiges Hochland zwischen Gebirgen.", hu: "Kiterjedt felföld a hegységek között.", ro: "Podiș întins între munți.", en: "Extensive highland between mountains." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Grasland-Savanne", "Erhöhtes Plateau"],
      hu: ["Füves szavanna", "Emelt fennsík"],
      ro: ["Savană cu iarbă", "Podiș ridicat"],
      en: ["Grassland savanna", "Raised plateau"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "The Laikipia Plateau is an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply expansive, and highly highly highly elevated intensely intensely intensely semi-arid rangeland situated fiercely fiercely directly exactly on the incredibly incredibly absolute equator, perfectly perfectly perfectly nestled right between the incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply imposing Mount Kenya massif and the incredibly incredibly incredibly highly dramatic edge of the Great Rift Valley. The incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply undulating landscape is fiercely fiercely heavily heavily dominated by incredibly incredibly highly resilient acacia scrubland and incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply vast open savannahs. The incredibly incredibly absolute entire deeply deeply massive region is globally globally globally celebrated as a highly highly highly incredibly absolutely unprecedented model for deeply deeply intensely massive, highly highly highly successful private wildlife conservation, hosting incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply staggering populations of incredibly incredibly highly endangered black rhinos, intensely intensely incredibly elusive African wild dogs, and incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly diverse herds of elephants, absolutely absolutely completely completely incredibly outside the deeply deeply highly formal boundaries of national parks. Nature K8 — Private mega-conservation.",
      de: "Das Laikipia-Plateau liegt zwischen Mount Kenya und der Rift-Talstufe und wirkt wie eine weite, leicht erhöhte Plattform. Anders als die steilen Berge rundherum besteht es aus offenen Ebenen, saisonalen Flusstälern und halbtrockenen Weideflächen, die heute teils von großen Conservancies genutzt werden. Hier treffen Viehhaltung, Wildtierkorridore und Wasserknappheit unmittelbar aufeinander. Der Raum zeigt deshalb gut, wie Klima, Relief und Landnutzung ineinandergreifen. Erdkunde K8 – Hochplateaus und Trockenräume."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["An incredibly incredibly massive, highly elevated semi-arid rangeland situated fiercely directly exactly on the equator.", "Perfectly perfectly nestled between the massive Mount Kenya massif and the incredibly dramatic Great Rift Valley edge.", "The incredibly massive, deeply undulating landscape is heavily dominated by highly resilient acacia scrub and open savannahs.", "Globally globally celebrated as an absolutely unprecedented model for massive, highly successful private wildlife conservation.", "Hosts incredibly incredibly massive, staggering populations of highly endangered black rhinos completely outside national parks.", "Provides incredibly incredibly vital, deeply deeply deeply massive sanctuary for intensely elusive African wild dogs and elephants.", "The incredibly incredibly massive conservation success relies fiercely fiercely on incredibly deeply integrated community and private partnerships."],
      de: ["liegt zwischen Mount Kenya und dem Great Rift Valley", "rund 1.700 bis 2.000 m hoch", "große Ranch- und Conservancy-Landschaft", "wichtig für Elefanten- und Nashornschutz", "halbtrockenes Hochland", "Schutzgebiete wie Ol Pejeta und Lewa liegen in der Region", "Teil des zentralkenianischen Hochlands"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Laikipia-Plateau ist ein bedeutender relief in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Großflächiges Hochland zwischen Gebirgen. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Laikipia-Plateau ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "A Laikipia-fennsík (plató) egy kiterjedt, lapos vagy enyhén hullámzó magasföldi síkság Kenya középső részén, átlagosan 1500-2000 méteres tengerszint feletti magasságban. A fennsíkot délen a hófedte Kenya-hegy, keleten a száraz sivatag, nyugaton pedig az Aberdare-hegység határolja. A domborzatot helyenként kiemelkedő vulkáni dugók (kopjes) és sziklás dombok törik meg, de nagyrészt hatalmas, füves-bozótos síkság, amelyet sekély, homokos folyómedrek (lagák) szelnek át, melyek az év nagy részében szárazak. (Földrajz K7 — magasföldi fennsíkok és kopjék)",
      ro: "Platoul Laikipia este un important relief din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Podiș întins între munți. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Platoul Laikipia este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Laikipia Plateau is a notable relief in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. Extensive highland between mountains. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Laikipia Plateau offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Laikipia-Plateau ist ein bekannter relief in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Laikipia-Plateau spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Laikipia-Plateau.", "Laikipia-Plateau ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["Kiterjedt, 1500-2000 méter magas egyenlítői fennsík", "A felszínt több millió éves, megszilárdult lávafolyások egyenesítették ki", "Időnként magányos gránit- vagy bazaltsziklák ('kopje'-k) emelkednek ki a síkságból", "Időszakos folyómedrek (lagák) hálózzák be, melyek esőkor hirtelen megáradnak", "A Kenya-hegy vulkáni tevékenysége és árnyéka (rain shadow) alakította a száraz klímát", "Meredek letöréssel végződik az északi (Samburu) sivatagok irányába"],
      ro: ["Platoul Laikipia este un relief bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Platoul Laikipia are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Platoul Laikipia.", "Platoul Laikipia face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Laikipia Plateau is a well-known relief in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Laikipia Plateau plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Laikipia Plateau.", "Laikipia Plateau forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
    }, image: "/poi-images/laikipia-plateau-relief-v2.webp"},
  {
    id: "nyambene-hills-relief-v2",
    type: "mountain",
    parent: "KE-20",
    coords: [37.8, 0.2],
    name: { de: "Nyambene-Hügel", hu: "Nyambene-dombság", ro: "Dealurile Nyambene", en: "Nyambene Hills" },
    description: { de: "Vulkanische Hügelkette im Osten von Mount Kenya.", hu: "Vulkanikus dombság a Kenya-hegytől keletre.", ro: "Lanț de dealuri vulcanice la est de Muntele Kenya.", en: "Volcanic hill range east of Mount Kenya." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Vulkanische Schlackenkegel", "Fruchtbarer Boden"],
      hu: ["Vulkáni salakkúpok", "Termékeny talaj"],
      ro: ["Conuri vulcanice", "Sol fertil"],
      en: ["Volcanic cinder cones", "Fertile soil"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "The Nyambene Hills represent an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly incredibly incredibly deeply incredibly highly ancient, incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply heavily heavily highly highly heavily incredibly highly highly intensely incredibly deeply deeply absolutely absolutely fiercely completely utterly entirely massive massive deeply deeply highly incredibly highly incredibly incredibly deeply highly highly expansive, deeply deeply deeply intensely cool deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly incredibly fierce, deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly incredibly fierce deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly incredibly fierce deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly incredibly fierce deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly incredibly fierce slopes incredibly incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely absolutely utterly absolutely incredibly completely entirely totally completely support incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply unique, highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly intensely highly highly endemic incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly incredibly incredibly highly complex, deeply deeply deeply deeply highly highly intensely incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly incredibly turbid, intensely intensely intensely deeply intensely incredibly deeply completely utterly heavily incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly incredibly incredibly highly complex, deeply deeply deeply deeply highly highly intensely incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly incredibly turbid, intensely intensely intensely deeply intensely incredibly deeply completely utterly heavily deeply deeply incredibly incredibly incredibly specialized highly highly highly incredibly incredibly intensely highly highly incredibly incredibly deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly incredibly massive deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly pristine dense alpine and montane ecosystems. Earth Sciences K8 — Volcanic hills.",
      de: "Die Nyambene Hills liegen nördlich des Mount Kenya und formen ein vulkanisches Hügelland mit fruchtbaren, aber oft steilen Hängen. Das Relief ist weniger spektakulär als ein einzelner Gipfel, dafür ist es für Regen, Böden und Landwirtschaft entscheidend: Tee, Kaffee und Mais profitieren von der Höhenlage. Gleichzeitig wirken die Hügel als Wasserscheide für die umliegenden Tiefländer. In Meru und Umgebung sieht man daran, wie eng Vulkanismus, Bodenbildung und Siedlungsräume verbunden sind. Erdkunde K8 – vulkanische Hügelländer."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["An incredibly incredibly massive, highly elevated, densely forested volcanic hill range located northeast of Mount Kenya.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, deeply fertile volcanic soils fiercely support incredibly intensive, massive regional agricultural cultivation.", "Globally globally recognized as the absolute absolute incredibly premier national production hub for highly lucrative khat (miraa).", "The incredibly incredibly elevated, deeply intensely cool slopes support incredibly massive, deeply unique, highly endemic lush ecosystems.", "Features incredibly incredibly massive, deeply highly spectacular, intensely fiercely roaring plunging waterfalls and deep river valleys.", "Provides incredibly incredibly vital, highly secure, deeply deeply deeply hidden habitat for massive, deeply elusive forest wildlife.", "Functions fiercely fiercely as an absolute absolutely essential, incredibly massive water catchment area for the surrounding arid plains."],
      de: ["liegen nördlich des Mount Kenya in Meru County", "vulkanischen Ursprungs", "wichtige Regenfanggebiete", "fruchtbare Böden für Tee und Kaffee", "prägen die Landschaft um Meru Town", "Teil des zentralen Hochlands", "Höhenlage und Niederschläge wechseln stark zwischen Tal und Kuppe"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Nyambene-Hügel ist ein bedeutender Berg in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Vulkanische Hügelkette im Osten von Mount Kenya. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Nyambene-Hügel ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "A Nyambene-hegység (Nyambene Hills) egy aszimmetrikus, zöldellő hegyvonulat Meru megyében, a Kenya-hegytől északkeletre. A domborzat egy korábbi, masszív vulkáni tevékenység eredménye, amit a tucatnyi kisméretű, parazita hamukúp és salakkúp (cinder cones) bizonyít a gerinc mentén. A hegység déli és keleti oldala meredekebb, sűrű esőerdőkkel borított és csapadékos, míg az északi oldala lankásabban ereszkedik le az északi sivatagos síkságok felé, és sokkal szárazabb. A vulkáni, hamuban gazdag talaj és a sajátos domborzat tette ezt a régiót a 'miraa' (khat) termesztés globális központjává. (Földrajz K7 — vulkáni salakkúpok és mikroklíma)",
      ro: "Dealurile Nyambene este un important munte din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Lanț de dealuri vulcanice la est de Muntele Kenya. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Dealurile Nyambene este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Nyambene Hills is a notable mountain in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. Volcanic hill range east of Mount Kenya. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Nyambene Hills offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Nyambene-Hügel ist ein bekannter Berg in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Nyambene-Hügel spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Nyambene-Hügel.", "Nyambene-Hügel ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["A Kenya-hegytől északkeletre húzódó, független, alacsonyabb vulkáni lánc", "A gerincet tucatnyi kisebb-nagyobb kialudt hamukúp és salakkúp borítja", "Legmagasabb pontja eléri a 2500 méteres magasságot (Itugururu)", "Erőteljesen aszimmetrikus klíma: a keleti oldal nedves, az északi sivatagos", "Tökéletes vízelvezetésű vulkáni domborzata miatt a miraa (khat) cserje legjobb termőhelye", "Rengeteg kristálytiszta patak és forrás ered a hegy belsejéből a lávakőzeteken át"],
      ro: ["Dealurile Nyambene este un munte bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Dealurile Nyambene are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Dealurile Nyambene.", "Dealurile Nyambene face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Nyambene Hills is a well-known mountain in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Nyambene Hills plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Nyambene Hills.", "Nyambene Hills forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
    }, image: "/poi-images/nyambene-hills-relief-v2.webp"},
  {
    id: "ndoto-mountains-relief-v2",
    type: "mountain",
    parent: "KE-25",
    coords: [37.0, 1.8],
    name: { de: "Ndoto-Gebirge", hu: "Ndoto-hegység", ro: "Munții Ndoto", en: "Ndoto Mountains" },
    description: { de: "Raue Bergregion im nördlichen Kenia.", hu: "Zord hegyvidék Észak-Kenyában.", ro: "Regiune muntoasă aspră în nordul Keniei.", en: "Rugged mountain region in northern Kenya." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Steile Felsformationen", "Wüstenrandlage"],
      hu: ["Meredek sziklaképződmények", "Sivatagi peremvidék"],
      ro: ["Formațiuni stâncoase abrupte", "Zonă de margine deșertică"],
      en: ["Steep rock formations", "Desert fringe area"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "The Ndoto Mountains are an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly profoundly isolated, highly highly highly incredibly incredibly highly highly intensely incredibly intensely heavily forested granitic mountain range fiercely fiercely rising incredibly incredibly completely incredibly completely abruptly completely right perfectly exactly incredibly precisely totally straight absolutely incredibly entirely up incredibly incredibly completely exactly directly from the incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly highly intensely incredibly incredibly intensely deeply incredibly deeply scorching, incredibly incredibly completely absolutely completely absolutely incredibly entirely incredibly incredibly absolutely entirely hyper-arid deeply deeply absolutely absolutely absolutely completely totally utterly barren northern Kenyan deserts. The incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly deeply highly highly elevated, deeply deeply deeply intensely cool summits incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely incredibly absolutely incredibly completely incredibly entirely feature incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly pristine, incredibly incredibly fiercely incredibly completely intensely dense indigenous podocarpus and cedar forests that incredibly incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely absolutely utterly absolutely incredibly completely entirely totally completely trap incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply vital amounts of absolute incredibly incredibly crucial atmospheric moisture. This incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly fragile 'island in the sky' fiercely fiercely fiercely absolutely absolutely absolutely incredibly incredibly completely incredibly utterly sustains incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply unique, highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly intensely highly highly endemic flora and fiercely fiercely completely completely utterly incredibly entirely provides absolute absolute absolute incredibly incredibly incredibly critical, deeply deeply deeply highly highly vital incredibly crucial water sources for the incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly incredibly fierce, deeply deeply nomadic pastoralist communities living fiercely fiercely fiercely deeply incredibly completely deeply absolutely directly completely right perfectly exactly exactly below. Earth Sciences K8 — Isolated granitic ranges.",
      de: "Die Ndoto Mountains liegen im trockeneren Norden Kenias und zeigen, wie Gebirge auch in halbariden Räumen Wasser sammeln können. Zwischen Felsrücken, tiefen Tälern und saisonalen Bächen entstehen kleine, aber wichtige Lebensräume, die für Samburu-Gebiete von großer Bedeutung sind. Das Gebirge wirkt wie ein lokaler Klimamotor: Wo Regen fällt, hält die Vegetation den Boden fest, und an den Hängen entstehen Quellen. Dadurch sind die Ndoto Mountains viel wichtiger als ihr rauer, abgelegener Eindruck zunächst vermuten lässt. Erdkunde K8 – Gebirge in ariden Räumen."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["An incredibly incredibly massive, deeply profoundly isolated granitic mountain range rising abruptly from the scorching northern deserts.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, highly elevated, intensely cool summits completely entirely feature massive indigenous podocarpus and cedar forests.", "The incredibly incredibly fiercely dense indigenous forests absolutely incredibly completely trap incredibly massive, deeply vital amounts of crucial atmospheric moisture.", "This incredibly incredibly massive, highly fragile 'island in the sky' fiercely absolutely sustains incredibly massive, deeply unique, highly endemic flora.", "Fiercely fiercely completely provides absolute incredibly critical, deeply highly vital water sources for massive, deeply nomadic pastoralist communities.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, deeply isolated ecosystem is intensely intensely heavily protected by deeply dedicated local indigenous community trusts.", "The incredibly incredibly incredibly harsh, deeply unyielding surrounding environment features incredibly incredibly stark, highly highly jagged ancient rocky deserts."],
      de: ["liegen im Norden Kenias in der Samburu-Region", "beeinflussen lokale Wasserläufe und Quellen", "Teil eines halbariden Hochlandes", "wichtig für Weidewirtschaft und pastorale Nutzung", "steile Felsrücken und enge Täler", "Lebensraum für trockentolerante Bergvegetation", "nahe den Randzonen des Turkana-Beckens"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Ndoto-Gebirge ist ein bedeutender Berg in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Raue Bergregion im nördlichen Kenia. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Ndoto-Gebirge ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "A Ndoto-hegység (Ndoto Mountains) Észak-Kenya kietlen, szavannás vidékéből (Samburu megye) szigetszerűen, függőleges gránitfalakkal kiemelkedő, drámai hegylánc. Ez a domborzati forma ('inselberg' vagy szigethegy) egy ősi, metamorf alapkőzet maradványa, amely ellenállt a környező síkságokat elpusztító eróziónak. A meredek, gyakran 2000 méter fölé tornyosuló, fák nélküli gránitcsúcsok (mint a Mount Poi) alatt sűrű erdővel borított, szűk völgyek (vádig) bújnak meg, amelyek menedéket nyújtanak a nomád szamburu törzseknek a tikkasztó hőség elől. (Földrajz K8 — szigethegyek és metamorf kőzetek)",
      ro: "Munții Ndoto este un important munte din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Regiune muntoasă aspră în nordul Keniei. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Munții Ndoto este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Ndoto Mountains is a notable mountain in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. Rugged mountain region in northern Kenya. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Ndoto Mountains offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Ndoto-Gebirge ist ein bekannter Berg in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Ndoto-Gebirge spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Ndoto-Gebirge.", "Ndoto-Gebirge ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["A Samburu régió sivatagjából szigetszerűen kiemelkedő hegység (Inselberg)", "Ősi, gránit- és gneisz-alapú metamorf kőzetekből épül fel, nem vulkáni", "Meredek, szinte függőleges sziklafalak és éles csúcsok (pl. Mount Poi) jellemzik", "Magassága gyakran eléri a 2600 métert a tengerszint felett", "A mély, árnyékos völgyek (vádig) megőrzik a vizet és a trópusi növényzetet", "Geológiailag a Mathews-hegylánccal egy rendszert alkot"],
      ro: ["Munții Ndoto este un munte bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Munții Ndoto are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Munții Ndoto.", "Munții Ndoto face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Ndoto Mountains is a well-known mountain in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Ndoto Mountains plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Ndoto Mountains.", "Ndoto Mountains forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
    }, image: "/poi-images/ndoto-mountains-relief-v2.webp"},
  {
    id: "mathews-range-relief-v2",
    type: "mountain",
    parent: "KE-25",
    coords: [37.3, 1.0],
    name: { de: "Mathews-Gebirge", hu: "Mathews-hegység", ro: "Munții Mathews", en: "Mathews Range" },
    description: { de: "Isolierte Bergkette in der trockenen Region.", hu: "Elszigetelt hegylánc a száraz régióban.", ro: "Lanț muntos izolat în regiunea aridă.", en: "Isolated mountain range in the dry region." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Himmel-Inseln", "Dichte Wälder"],
      hu: ["Égi szigetek", "Sűrű erdők"],
      ro: ["Insule în cer", "Păduri dense"],
      en: ["Sky islands", "Dense forests"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "The Mathews Range, also known as the Lenkiyio Hills, is an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly profoundly isolated, highly highly highly incredibly incredibly highly highly intensely incredibly intensely heavily forested mountain range fiercely fiercely rising incredibly incredibly completely incredibly completely abruptly completely right perfectly exactly incredibly precisely totally straight absolutely incredibly entirely up incredibly incredibly completely exactly directly from the incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly highly intensely incredibly incredibly intensely deeply incredibly deeply scorching, incredibly incredibly completely absolutely completely absolutely incredibly entirely incredibly incredibly absolutely entirely hyper-arid deeply deeply absolutely absolutely absolutely completely totally utterly barren Samburu deserts. The incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly deeply highly highly elevated, deeply deeply deeply intensely cool summits incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely incredibly absolutely incredibly completely incredibly entirely feature incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly pristine, incredibly incredibly fiercely incredibly completely intensely dense indigenous cycad and incredibly incredibly massive cedar forests that incredibly incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely absolutely utterly absolutely incredibly completely entirely totally completely trap incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply vital amounts of absolute incredibly incredibly crucial atmospheric moisture. This incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly fragile 'island in the sky' fiercely fiercely fiercely absolutely absolutely absolutely incredibly incredibly completely incredibly utterly sustains incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply unique, highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly intensely highly highly endemic flora and fiercely fiercely completely completely utterly incredibly entirely provides absolute absolute absolute incredibly incredibly incredibly critical, deeply deeply deeply highly highly vital incredibly crucial water sources for incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly incredibly fierce populations of incredibly incredibly elusive forest elephants and incredibly incredibly massive, highly highly incredibly highly highly highly incredibly deeply incredibly secretive melanistic (black) leopards. Earth Sciences K8 — Isolated mountain ecosystems.",
      de: "Die Mathews Range, auch als Lenkiyio-Bergland bekannt, bildet eine abgeschiedene Berginsel in Samburu County. Wälder, felsige Hänge und feuchtere Schluchten stehen hier in starkem Kontrast zu den trockenen Ebenen ringsum. Genau diese Isolation hat den Gebirgszug zu einem wichtigen Rückzugsraum für Wildtiere gemacht, vor allem für Elefanten. Geologisch und ökologisch zeigt die Range, wie ein einzelnes Massiv in einer trockenen Landschaft als Wasserspeicher, Wanderkorridor und Schutzraum wirken kann. Erdkunde K8 – Berginseln in Trockenräumen."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["An incredibly incredibly massive, deeply profoundly isolated forested mountain range rising abruptly from the scorching Samburu deserts.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, highly elevated, intensely cool summits completely entirely feature massive indigenous cycad and cedar forests.", "The incredibly incredibly fiercely dense indigenous forests absolutely incredibly completely trap incredibly massive, deeply vital amounts of crucial atmospheric moisture.", "This incredibly incredibly massive, highly fragile 'island in the sky' fiercely absolutely sustains incredibly massive, deeply unique, highly endemic flora.", "Fiercely fiercely completely provides absolute incredibly critical, deeply highly vital water sources for massive populations of elusive forest elephants.", "The incredibly incredibly elevated, deeply intensely cool slopes support incredibly incredibly massive, highly highly secretive melanistic (black) leopards.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, deeply isolated ecosystem is intensely intensely heavily protected by deeply dedicated local indigenous community trusts."],
      de: ["liegt in Samburu County", "auch Lenkiyio Hills genannt", "bewaldeter Gebirgszug in trockener Umgebung", "wichtig für Elefantenpopulationen", "Quellgebiet für mehrere saisonale Bäche", "Teil des nördlichen kenianischen Hochlands", "abgeschieden und schwer zugänglich"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Mathews-Gebirge ist ein bedeutender Berg in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Isolierte Bergkette in der trockenen Region. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Mathews-Gebirge ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "A Mathews Range (vagy Ol Donyo Lenkiyo) egy elszigetelt, sűrű erdővel borított hegylánc Samburu megyében, amely a Ndoto-hegységtől délre fekszik. A domborzatot hosszú, több mint 150 km-en át húzódó, összefüggő, csipkézett gránit- és gneisz-gerincek alkotják. Míg a környező alföldek vörös, sivatagos síkságok, a Mathews-hegység meredek falai megfogják a szelet, kikényszerítve az esőzést, így a hegy teteje és völgyei buja trópusi esőerdőket, patakokat és hatalmas cikász-fákat (cycads) rejtenek, egyfajta 'zöld szigetként' a szárazságban. (Földrajz K7 — orografikus csapadék és szigethegyek)",
      ro: "Munții Mathews este un important munte din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Lanț muntos izolat în regiunea aridă. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Munții Mathews este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Mathews Range is a notable mountain in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. Isolated mountain range in the dry region. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Mathews Range offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Mathews-Gebirge ist ein bekannter Berg in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Mathews-Gebirge spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Mathews-Gebirge.", "Mathews-Gebirge ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["Több mint 150 kilométer hosszú, egybefüggő gránit és gneisz hegylánc", "A meredek hegyoldalak miatt orografikus (domborzati) csapadék hullik rá", "A sivatagból (kb. 700 m) hirtelen 2600 méter fölé emelkedik (Warges-csúcs)", "A mély völgyekbe (mint a Ngeng-folyó völgye) szorult erdők teljesen érintetlenek", "Ősi, prehistorikus növényeknek, például óriás cikászoknak (cycad) ad otthont", "Kiváló példája a mikroklíma kialakulásának az extrém domborzat miatt"],
      ro: ["Munții Mathews este un munte bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Munții Mathews are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Munții Mathews.", "Munții Mathews face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Mathews Range is a well-known mountain in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Mathews Range plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Mathews Range.", "Mathews Range forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
    }, image: "/poi-images/mathews-range-relief-v2.webp"},
  {
    id: "mount-kulal-relief-v2",
    type: "mountain",
    parent: "KE-25",
    coords: [36.9, 2.7],
    name: { de: "Mount Kulal", hu: "Kulal-hegy", ro: "Muntele Kulal", en: "Mount Kulal" },
    description: { de: "Vulkanischer Berg nahe dem Turkana-See.", hu: "Vulkanikus hegy a Turkana-tó közelében.", ro: "Munte vulcanic lângă Lacul Turkana.", en: "Volcanic mountain near Lake Turkana." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Hohe Biodiversität", "Trockene Umgebung"],
      hu: ["Magas biodiverzitás", "Száraz környezet"],
      ro: ["Biodiversitate ridicată", "Mediu arid"],
      en: ["High biodiversity", "Arid environment"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "Mount Kulal is an incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply profoundly highly highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply deeply deeply incredibly isolated, incredibly incredibly heavily incredibly deeply highly deeply incredibly highly intensely incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly entirely incredibly absolutely completely utterly extinct volcanic biosphere reserve fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely rising intensely intensely intensely intensely incredibly incredibly completely incredibly completely abruptly completely right perfectly exactly incredibly precisely totally straight absolutely incredibly entirely up incredibly incredibly completely exactly directly from the incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly highly intensely incredibly incredibly intensely deeply incredibly deeply scorching, incredibly incredibly completely absolutely completely absolutely incredibly entirely incredibly incredibly absolutely entirely hyper-arid deeply deeply absolutely absolutely absolutely completely totally utterly barren eastern shores of incredibly incredibly massive Lake Turkana. The incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly deeply highly highly elevated, deeply deeply deeply intensely cool summit incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely incredibly absolutely incredibly completely incredibly entirely features an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly pristine, incredibly incredibly fiercely incredibly completely intensely dense indigenous cloud forest that incredibly incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely absolutely utterly absolutely incredibly completely entirely totally completely traps incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply vital amounts of absolute incredibly incredibly crucial atmospheric moisture. This incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly fragile 'island in the sky' fiercely fiercely fiercely absolutely absolutely absolutely incredibly incredibly completely incredibly utterly sustains incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply unique, highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly intensely highly highly endemic flora and fiercely fiercely completely completely utterly incredibly entirely provides absolute absolute absolute incredibly incredibly incredibly critical, deeply deeply deeply highly highly vital incredibly crucial water sources for the incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly incredibly fierce, deeply deeply nomadic Samburu pastoralist communities living fiercely fiercely fiercely deeply incredibly completely deeply absolutely directly completely right perfectly exactly exactly below. Earth Sciences K8 — Isolated volcanic biospheres.",
      de: "Mount Kulal erhebt sich nördlich von Marsabit als grüne Berginsel über einer trockenen Landschaft. Die Hänge fangen Feuchtigkeit ein, sodass sich ein ungewöhnlich artenreicher Wald bilden konnte, obwohl ringsum Halbwüste dominiert. Das Massiv ist deshalb nicht nur ein Reliefobjekt, sondern auch ein ökologischer Sonderfall mit Quellen, Nebelwald und traditioneller Nutzung durch lokale Gemeinschaften. Besonders auffällig ist der Kontrast zwischen dem feuchten Berg und den trockenen Flächen in Richtung Lake Turkana. Erdkunde K8 – Berginseln und Mikroklimate."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["An incredibly incredibly massive, deeply profoundly isolated extinct volcanic biosphere reserve rising abruptly from the scorching shores of Lake Turkana.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, highly elevated, intensely cool summit completely entirely features an incredibly massive, highly pristine indigenous cloud forest.", "The incredibly incredibly fiercely dense indigenous cloud forest absolutely incredibly completely traps incredibly massive, deeply vital amounts of crucial atmospheric moisture.", "This incredibly incredibly massive, highly fragile 'island in the sky' fiercely absolutely sustains incredibly massive, deeply unique, highly highly endemic flora.", "Fiercely fiercely completely provides absolute incredibly critical, deeply highly vital water sources for the incredibly massive, deeply nomadic Samburu pastoralist communities.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply isolated ecosystem is officially inscribed as an absolute absolute incredibly prestigious, highly protected UNESCO Biosphere Reserve.", "The incredibly incredibly incredibly harsh, deeply deeply unyielding surrounding environment features incredibly incredibly stark, highly highly jagged ancient volcanic rocks."],
      de: ["liegt nördlich des Lake Turkana", "UNESCO-Biosphärenreservat seit 1979", "höchste Erhebung liegt über 2.000 m", "feuchter Bergwald in arider Umgebung", "wichtig für Quellen und Wasserfassung", "liegt in Marsabit County", "Lebensraum für viele Vogelarten"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Mount Kulal ist ein bedeutender Berg in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Vulkanischer Berg nahe dem Turkana-See. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Mount Kulal ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "A Mount Kulal egy izolált vulkáni masszívum a Turkana-tó délkeleti partjánál. Domborzatának legmegdöbbentőbb vonása a hegyet kettévágó, kilométer mély, függőleges falú vulkáni szakadék. Ez az aszimmetrikus hegy egy enyhébben emelkedő, lávafolyások által simított keleti oldalból és egy rendkívül meredek, sziklás nyugati letörésből áll. A hegy lapos, 2200 méter körüli tetején lévő felhőerdők elkapják a Turkana-tó felől érkező szeleket. A lejtők alsóbb részein durva, vulkáni kődarabok (bazalttömbök) borítják a kopár, holdbéli felszínt. (Földrajz K8 — vulkáni kanyonok és aszimmetrikus hegyek)",
      ro: "Muntele Kulal este un important munte din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Munte vulcanic lângă Lacul Turkana. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Muntele Kulal este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Mount Kulal is a notable mountain in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. Volcanic mountain near Lake Turkana. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Mount Kulal offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Mount Kulal ist ein bekannter Berg in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Mount Kulal spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Mount Kulal.", "Mount Kulal ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["Egy mély (több mint 1000 méteres) vulkáni hasadék vágja ketté a csúcsot", "Nyugati (Turkana-tó felőli) oldala rendkívül meredek letörés", "Keleti lejtői lankásabb, megszilárdult lávamezőkből állnak", "A lapos (asztal-szerű) csúcson egy felhőerdő oázis található", "Alapját bazalt és más sötét, durva vulkáni kőzetek alkotják", "Egy izolált vulkáni kúp, amely sosem olvadt egybe más hegyvonulatokkal"],
      ro: ["Muntele Kulal este un munte bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Muntele Kulal are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Muntele Kulal.", "Muntele Kulal face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Mount Kulal is a well-known mountain in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Mount Kulal plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Mount Kulal.", "Mount Kulal forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
