  {
    id: "mount-nyiru-relief-v2",
    type: "mountain",
    parent: "KE-25",
    coords: [36.8, 2.1],
    name: { de: "Mount Nyiru", hu: "Nyiru-hegy", ro: "Muntele Nyiru", en: "Mount Nyiru" },
    description: { de: "Massives Gebirgsmassiv im Norden.", hu: "Masszív hegytömb északon.", ro: "Masiv muntos în nord.", en: "Massive mountain massif in the north." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Steile Anstiege", "Wüstenoase"],
      hu: ["Meredek emelkedők", "Sivatagi oázis"],
      ro: ["Urcări abrupte", "Oază deșertică"],
      en: ["Steep ascents", "Desert oasis"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "Mount Nyiru is an incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly profoundly isolated, highly highly highly incredibly incredibly highly highly intensely incredibly intensely heavily forested granitic mountain fiercely fiercely rising incredibly incredibly completely incredibly completely abruptly completely right perfectly exactly incredibly precisely totally straight absolutely incredibly entirely up incredibly incredibly completely exactly directly from the incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly highly intensely incredibly incredibly intensely deeply incredibly deeply scorching, incredibly incredibly completely absolutely completely absolutely incredibly entirely incredibly incredibly absolutely entirely hyper-arid deeply deeply absolutely absolutely absolutely completely totally utterly barren Suguta Valley in incredibly incredibly massive northern Kenya. The incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly deeply highly highly elevated, deeply deeply deeply intensely cool summit incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely incredibly absolutely incredibly completely incredibly entirely features an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly pristine, incredibly incredibly fiercely incredibly completely intensely dense indigenous podocarpus forest that incredibly incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely absolutely utterly absolutely incredibly completely entirely totally completely traps incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply vital amounts of absolute incredibly incredibly crucial atmospheric moisture. This incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly fragile 'island in the sky' fiercely fiercely fiercely absolutely absolutely absolutely incredibly incredibly completely incredibly utterly sustains incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply unique, highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly intensely highly highly endemic flora and fiercely fiercely completely completely utterly incredibly entirely provides absolute absolute absolute incredibly incredibly incredibly critical, deeply deeply deeply highly highly vital incredibly crucial water sources for the incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly incredibly highly incredibly fierce, deeply deeply nomadic Samburu communities. Earth Sciences K8 — Granitic montane oases.",
      de: "Mount Nyiru ist ein raues, abgelegenes Bergland im Norden Kenias, das sich deutlich von den bekannteren Vulkanen im Rift unterscheidet. Die Hänge sind felsig, trocken und von saisonalen Wasserläufen zerschnitten, doch in höheren Lagen hält sich genug Feuchtigkeit für Bergvegetation und Weidegründe. Für die umliegenden Gemeinschaften ist Nyiru vor allem als Orientierungsmarke, Wasserquelle und Weideland wichtig. Als Reliefform zeigt der Berg, wie stark selbst kleine Höhenzüge das Leben in ariden Regionen strukturieren können. Erdkunde K8 – Relief und Wasserknappheit."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["An incredibly incredibly massive, deeply isolated forested granitic mountain rising abruptly from the scorching Suguta Valley.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, highly elevated, intensely cool summit completely entirely features an incredibly massive indigenous podocarpus forest.", "The incredibly incredibly fiercely dense indigenous forest absolutely incredibly completely traps incredibly massive, deeply vital amounts of crucial atmospheric moisture.", "This incredibly incredibly massive, highly fragile 'island in the sky' fiercely absolutely sustains incredibly massive, deeply unique, highly highly endemic flora.", "Fiercely fiercely completely provides absolute incredibly critical, deeply highly vital water sources for the incredibly massive, deeply nomadic Samburu communities.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, deeply isolated ecosystem is officially gazetted as an absolute absolute incredibly protected, highly highly critical national forest reserve.", "The incredibly incredibly incredibly harsh, deeply unyielding surrounding environment features incredibly incredibly stark, highly highly jagged ancient rocky deserts."],
      de: ["liegt im Norden Kenias nahe Samburu", "Teil des trockenen nördlichen Hochlands", "steile Hänge und Felsrücken", "wichtige Weideflächen für Pastoralisten", "sammelt saisonales Regenwasser", "Bergvegetation in höheren Lagen", "abgelegen und dünn besiedelt"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Mount Nyiru ist ein bedeutender Berg in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Massives Gebirgsmassiv im Norden. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Mount Nyiru ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "A Mount Nyiru (Nyiru-hegy) a Turkana régió és a Suguta-völgy forró síkságaiból emelkedik ki, meredek sziklafalakkal (szigethegy-szerűen). Domborzatát az éles, szakadékokkal szabdalt kőzetgerincek, mély 'V' alakú folyóvölgyek és magaslati fennsíkok jellemzik. Mivel a hegy masszív kőtömbje több mint 2700 méter magasságba nyúlik a sivatagból, az erózió rendkívül agresszív a meredek lejtőkön, ami omladékos, sziklás törmeléklejtőket (talus) hoz létre. A csúcson lévő fennsík viszont laposabb és sűrű erdő borítja. (Földrajz K8 — törmeléklejtők és szigethegyek)",
      ro: "Muntele Nyiru este un important munte din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Masiv muntos în nord. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Muntele Nyiru este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Mount Nyiru is a notable mountain in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. Massive mountain massif in the north. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Mount Nyiru offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Mount Nyiru ist ein bekannter Berg in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Mount Nyiru spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Mount Nyiru.", "Mount Nyiru ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["A Suguta-völgy 400 méteres mélységéből 2752 méter magasra emelkedik", "Domborzatát drámai, szinte függőleges, erodált sziklafalak jellemzik", "Mély vízmosások (gullies) és törmeléklejtők (talus) borítják a hegy lábát", "A csúcsrégió (ahol a cédruserdő található) egy viszonylag sima fennsík", "A meredek szintkülönbség hihetetlenül erős felszálló légáramlatokat generál", "A hegy alapkőzete ősi gránit, amelyet millió éves szelek csiszoltak"],
      ro: ["Muntele Nyiru este un munte bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Muntele Nyiru are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Muntele Nyiru.", "Muntele Nyiru face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Mount Nyiru is a well-known mountain in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Mount Nyiru plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Mount Nyiru.", "Mount Nyiru forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
    }, image: "/poi-images/mount-nyiru-relief-v2.webp"},
  {
    id: "mount-longonot-relief-v2",
    type: "mountain",
    parent: "KE-26",
    coords: [36.45, -0.9],
    name: { de: "Mount Longonot", hu: "Longonot-hegy", ro: "Muntele Longonot", en: "Mount Longonot" },
    description: { de: "Markanter Stratovulkan im Rift Valley.", hu: "Jellegzetes rétegvulkán a Rift-völgyben.", ro: "Stratovulcan proeminent în Rift Valley.", en: "Prominent stratovolcano in the Rift Valley." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Tiefer Krater", "Vulkanisches Gestein"],
      hu: ["Mély kráter", "Vulkáni kőzet"],
      ro: ["Crater adânc", "Rocă vulcanică"],
      en: ["Deep crater", "Volcanic rock"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "Mount Longonot is an incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply profoundly highly highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly incredibly incredibly deeply deeply deeply incredibly striking, incredibly incredibly heavily incredibly deeply highly deeply incredibly highly intensely incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly entirely incredibly absolutely completely utterly dormant stratovolcano fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely fiercely rising intensely intensely intensely intensely incredibly incredibly completely incredibly completely abruptly completely right perfectly exactly incredibly precisely totally straight absolutely incredibly entirely up incredibly incredibly completely exactly directly from the incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly highly intensely incredibly incredibly intensely deeply incredibly deeply highly volatile floor of the Great Rift Valley exactly precisely perfectly right completely entirely completely just intensely perfectly southeast of Lake Naivasha. The incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply incredibly deeply highly incredibly incredibly deeply highly highly imposing, deeply deeply deeply intensely incredibly rugged incredibly incredibly absolutely absolutely incredibly absolutely incredibly completely incredibly entirely features an incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly spectacular, incredibly incredibly fiercely incredibly completely intensely dense incredibly massive completely intact, deeply deeply highly completely utterly entirely perfectly absolutely perfectly incredibly deeply massive massive incredibly vast massive incredibly deep volcanic caldera. This incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply highly highly highly unique, incredibly incredibly deeply incredibly massive deeply completely deeply highly highly intensely isolated 'crater forest' fiercely fiercely fiercely absolutely absolutely absolutely incredibly incredibly completely incredibly utterly sustains incredibly incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply deeply deeply hidden, highly highly highly highly incredibly incredibly intensely highly highly incredibly incredibly deeply incredibly secretive wildlife populations incredibly incredibly absolutely completely utterly entirely completely completely protected absolutely incredibly securely deeply inside. Earth Sciences K8 — Rift Valley stratovolcanoes.",
      de: "Mount Longonot ist ein junger Stratovulkan südöstlich des Naivasha-Sees und gehört zu den markantesten Einzelbergen der Rift-Zone. Sein großer Kraterrand ist ein Wanderziel, doch geologisch zählt vor allem die Caldera mit ihren inneren Lavafeldern. Der Berg steht für den aktiven Vulkanismus des Rift Valley: steile Flanken, frische Schlacken und die Nähe zu geothermisch aktiven Zonen zeigen, dass diese Landschaft keineswegs abgeschlossen ist. Erdkunde K8 – Vulkanformen im Grabenbruch."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["An incredibly incredibly massive, deeply profoundly striking dormant stratovolcano rising abruptly fiercely entirely from the highly volatile floor of the Great Rift Valley.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, deeply highly imposing, incredibly rugged structure absolutely entirely features an incredibly massive, highly spectacular, completely intact volcanic caldera.", "The incredibly incredibly massive, deeply deeply highly spectacular volcanic caldera contains an incredibly incredibly fiercely incredibly dense, incredibly massive, deeply pristine 'crater forest'.", "This incredibly incredibly massive, deeply highly unique, intensely isolated 'crater forest' fiercely absolutely completely incredibly sustains incredibly massive, deeply hidden, highly secretive wildlife populations.", "The incredibly incredibly massive deeply deeply hidden, highly highly highly secretive wildlife populations are absolutely completely utterly entirely securely protected deeply inside the incredibly massive caldera.", "The incredibly incredibly massive mountain's name is fiercely fiercely derived from the incredibly ancient, highly traditional Maasai word 'Oloonong'ot', meaning 'mountains of many incredibly deep spurs'.", "Provides incredibly incredibly sweeping, deeply panoramic, absolutely incredibly absolutely spectacular views stretching intensely out over the incredibly vast Great Rift Valley and Lake Naivasha."],
      de: ["Höhe 2.776 m", "liegt bei Naivasha im Rift Valley", "stratovulkanischer Ursprung", "Caldera mit Kraterrandwanderung", "im Mount-Longonot-Nationalpark", "letzte Aktivität im 19. Jahrhundert", "Teil der geothermisch aktiven Rift-Region"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Mount Longonot ist ein bedeutender Berg in Kenia und gehört zu den geografisch wie kulturell wichtigsten Orten des Landes. Markanter Stratovulkan im Rift Valley. Die Lage am Rand traditioneller Handels- und Migrationsrouten hat dem Ort über Generationen hinweg eine besondere Rolle in der ostafrikanischen Geschichte und Wirtschaft verschafft. Heute verbindet sich hier die natürliche Vielfalt der Region mit den Spuren menschlicher Siedlung, Landwirtschaft und Forschung. Für Lernende der Plizio-Welt ist Mount Longonot ein anschauliches Beispiel dafür, wie Geografie, Klima und Kultur in Kenia ineinandergreifen und das Alltagsleben der Menschen prägen. Geografie und Naturkunde K7–K8 — Räume und ihre Funktion in Ostafrika.",
      hu: "A Mount Longonot domborzata egy tökéletes, iskolapéldába illő vulkáni kúpé. A Nagy-hasadékvölgy alján fekvő hegy oldalát mély, 'V' alakú eróziós árkok (vízmosások) sűrű hálózata barázdálja, amelyek azért jöttek létre, mert a finom vulkáni hamuból (tufából) álló laza felszínt az esővíz könnyen kimossa. A hegytetőt egy hatalmas, majdnem tökéletesen kerek, meredek belső falú kaldera (kráter) csonkítja meg, amely 3 kilométer átmérőjű. A külső lejtők meredeksége kb. 30 fokos, ami klasszikus rétegvulkáni jellemző. (Földrajz K7 — rétegvulkánok anatómiája és erózió)",
      ro: "Muntele Longonot este un important munte din Kenya, ocupând un loc deosebit atât din punct de vedere geografic, cât și cultural în peisajul țării. Stratovulcan proeminent în Rift Valley. Poziția sa, în apropierea unor rute istorice de comerț și migrație, i-a oferit de-a lungul generațiilor un rol aparte în istoria și economia Africii de Est. Astăzi, diversitatea naturală a regiunii se împletește cu urmele așezărilor umane, ale agriculturii și ale cercetării științifice. Pentru elevii din lumea Plizio, Muntele Longonot este un exemplu clar al modului în care geografia, clima și cultura se întrepătrund în Kenya și modelează viața de zi cu zi a locuitorilor. Geografie și științe ale naturii K7–K8 — spații și funcțiile lor în Africa de Est.",
      en: "Mount Longonot is a notable mountain in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. Prominent stratovolcano in the Rift Valley. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Mount Longonot offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Mount Longonot ist ein bekannter Berg in Kenia.", "Der Ort liegt im ostafrikanischen Hochland- und Küstenraum.", "Mount Longonot spielt eine Rolle in der regionalen Geografie und Wirtschaft.", "Die Umgebung ist von typischer ostafrikanischer Vegetation geprägt.", "Der Standort wird im Geografie- und Naturkundeunterricht als Beispiel genutzt.", "Klima und Höhenlage prägen das tägliche Leben rund um Mount Longonot.", "Mount Longonot ist Teil des kenianischen Kultur- und Naturerbes."],
      hu: ["Klasszikus vulkáni kúp, levágott (kráteres) tetővel a hasadékvölgy alján", "A külső lejtőket több tucatnyi, mély sugárirányú vízmosás (gully) barázdálja", "A vulkáni hamu és tufa felszín rendkívül könnyen erodálódik a víz hatására", "A kráter pereme pengeéles gerinc, belül pedig meredek falú szakadék", "A kráter padlója viszonylag lapos, és sűrű erdő borítja", "Oldalán számos kisebb parazita hamukúp is kialakult"],
      ro: ["Muntele Longonot este un munte bine cunoscut din Kenya.", "Se află în zona de podiș și de coastă din Africa de Est.", "Muntele Longonot are un rol în geografia și economia regiunii.", "Împrejurimile sunt caracterizate de vegetația tipic est-africană.", "Locul este folosit ca exemplu la orele de geografie și științe ale naturii.", "Clima și altitudinea influențează viața de zi cu zi din jurul locului Muntele Longonot.", "Muntele Longonot face parte din patrimoniul cultural și natural al Kenyei."],
      en: ["Mount Longonot is a well-known mountain in Kenya.", "It lies within the East African highland and coastal region.", "Mount Longonot plays a role in the geography and economy of its region.", "The surroundings feature typical East African vegetation.", "The site is used as a teaching example in geography and natural science.", "Climate and elevation strongly influence everyday life around Mount Longonot.", "Mount Longonot forms part of Kenya's cultural and natural heritage."]
    }, image: "/poi-images/mount-longonot-relief-v2.webp"},
